Pass a thread's stack size to the worker that runs it

Builder::stack_size is accepted and dropped, so every thread gets the stack
size wasm-bindgen gives a thread by default, however deep the recursion it
runs. The size travels with the module and memory in the worker's
initialization message, rounded up to whole WebAssembly pages as
wasm-bindgen requires, and the worker templates hand it to the shim's init
as thread_stack_size. A size of zero, which wasm-bindgen refuses, leaves
the thread that default.

